# 7. PERFORMANCE — ABSOLUTELY CRITICAL

The Liquid Glass visual style must not cause noticeable performance degradation.

A beautiful interface that is slow, laggy, battery-intensive, or memory-heavy is unacceptable.

Treat performance as a non-negotiable engineering requirement.

## Performance principles

1. Never apply expensive blur to every UI element.
2. Avoid multiple nested real-time blur layers.
3. Avoid full-screen blur unless strictly necessary.
4. Avoid continuously running animations.
5. Avoid unnecessary recompositions.
6. Avoid large unoptimized images.
7. Avoid unnecessary GPU effects.
8. Avoid excessive shadows.
9. Avoid unnecessary background services.
10. Avoid expensive calculations during UI rendering.

## Efficient Liquid Glass implementation

Use a performance-aware combination of:

- Pre-rendered glass textures where appropriate.
- Static translucent surfaces.
- Gradient highlights.
- Lightweight borders.
- Efficient alpha compositing.
- Carefully limited blur.
- Reusable Compose modifiers.
- Cached visual resources.
- Hardware-accelerated rendering where appropriate.
- Optimized vector assets.

Use real-time blur only for selected important components when it is supported and efficient.

Do not assume that every Android version supports the same blur APIs.

Use compatible fallbacks.

For example:

- Modern devices may use supported background blur for selected overlays.
- Older devices should use carefully designed translucent surfaces and static highlights.

The visual identity must remain consistent even when blur is reduced.

Do not create expensive shaders or custom rendering pipelines unless they provide a measurable benefit.

## Animation performance

Use short, smooth, intentional animations.

Prefer:

- Alpha transitions.
- Lightweight scale animations.
- Efficient progress animations.
- Subtle elevation changes.
- Small motion transitions.

Do not animate every glass reflection continuously.

Do not use perpetual shimmer effects.

Respect system animation and reduced-motion settings.

## Device targets

Optimize for ordinary mid-range Android phones.

Prioritize:

- Smooth scrolling.
- Fast startup.
- Low RAM consumption.
- Low CPU usage.
- Low battery consumption.
- Efficient image loading.
- Responsive navigation.
- Efficient database queries.

Target a smooth 60 FPS experience on supported mid-range devices.

Measure actual performance where profiling tools are available.

Never claim measured performance without measurements.

If a visual effect causes lag, simplify the implementation while preserving the Liquid Glass appearance.

